  "id": "prob_60",
  "numId": 60,
  "title": "Debug: 4-Bit Adder-Subtractor Not Subtracting",
  "description": "The pre-wired circuit should work as a 4-bit adder-subtractor: R = P + Q when S = 0 and R = P - Q when S = 1. Addition works perfectly, but subtraction always gives a wrong answer that is exactly one less than expected, and the most significant bit is never complemented. The faults are: (1) the Q3 line is connected straight to the 7483 instead of passing through its XOR gate, (2) the Carry-In of the 7483 is tied to GND instead of the select line S, and (3) the GND pin of the 7486 IC is not connected. Find and repair all three faults.",
  "difficulty": "Medium",
  "category": "debug",
  "tags": [
    "Debugging",
    "Adder-Subtractor",
    "7483",
    "7486",
    "2's Complement"
  ],
